{"step_index":512,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:58:13Z","input_tokens":2433,"cache_read_tokens":110997,"output_tokens":876,"content":"The **MANDATORY RULES** and `sanitize_invoice_data` cleaning pipeline have been added to the backend and integrated into the invoice processing flow.\n\n### 🛡️ Implementation Details\n\n1. **Backend Cleaning Function ([`utils/clean_items.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py))**:\n   - Added `sanitize_invoice_data(data: dict) -> dict` implementing:\n     - **Supplier Name Cleaning**: Strips `Phone`, `Mobile`, `Tel`, `Email`, `Mob` artifacts, numbers, and dangling separators with `re.sub(r'(Phone|Mobile|Tel|Email|Mob)[\\s:]*[\\+\\d\\s\\w@\\.\\-]+', '', supplier, flags=re.IGNORECASE).strip()`. Defaults to `\"Supplier Name Unclear\"` if empty.\n     - **Address & Metadata Filtering**: Discards rows containing address keywords (`plot`, `sector`, `industrial area`, `bazaar`, `road`, `street`, `haryana`, `delhi`, `gstin`, `gtin`, `state`, `thirteen`, `thousand`, `hundred`, `only`, `rupees`, `bank`, `ifsc`, `a/c`, `ac no`, `phone`) or description length $< 3$.\n     - **GSTIN, PAN & Tax Identifier Purging**: Filters out raw GSTIN strings, PAN strings, and alphanumeric ID tokens.\n     - **Positive Checks**: Requires quantity $> 0$ and unit rate $> 0$.\n     - **Pin Code / Corrupt Billed Ratio Check**: Rejects lines if `billed > (qty * rate * 10) and billed > 100000` (e.g. Sonipat pin code `131001` or corrupt scans).\n\n2. **Backend Server Integration ([`server.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py))**:\n   - In `/api/process-invoice`, `sanitize_invoice_data` runs on `extracted_data` immediately before the response is returned to the frontend.\n   - Recalculates genuine subtotal and totals based only on sanitized items.\n\n3. **OCR / AI System Instructions ([`utils/aiExtractor.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js))**:\n   - Updated `GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION` with the exact mandatory rules for Supplier Name, what constitutes a line item, and absolute forbidden items (addresses, plots, GSTIN/PAN strings, pincodes, telephone numbers, amount in words, and bank details).\n\n4. **Frontend Pipeline ([`app.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/app.js) & [`utils/privacyMasker.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/privacyMasker.js))**:\n   - `handleFileUpload()` routes extracted documents through the backend's `/api/process-invoice` route to ensure `sanitize_invoice_data` is always executed prior to recalculation and display.\n   - Client-side sanitizer (`sanitizeInvoiceData` in [`utils/privacyMasker.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/privacyMasker.js)) mirrors the exact same rules for offline resilience.\n\nThe server is active and running on **http://localhost:3000**."}
{"step_index":513,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T17:04:10Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nReplace the invoice upload backend endpoint completely with this robust FastAPI + Google GenAI implementation:\n\n1. Accept the file via UploadFile.\n2. Read the raw bytes and pass them directly as an inline image/PDF to 'gemini-2.5-flash'.\n3. Use this exact Pydantic schema and system prompt:\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom google import genai\nfrom google.genai import types\n\nclass InvoiceItem(BaseModel):\n    description: str\n    quantity: float\n    unit_rate: float\n    total_amount: float\n\nclass ExtractedInvoice(BaseModel):\n    is_valid_bill: bool\n    vendor_name: Optional[str]\n    gstin: Optional[str]\n    invoice_number: Optional[str]\n    date: Optional[str]\n    items: List[InvoiceItem]\n    subtotal: Optional[float]\n    cgst: Optional[float]\n    sgst: Optional[float]\n    igst: Optional[float]\n    declared_total: Optional[float]\n\n@app.post(\"/api/analyze-bill\")\nasync def analyze_bill(file: UploadFile = File(...)):\n    contents = await file.read()\n    mime_type = file.content_type or \"image/jpeg\"\n    \n    prompt = \"\"\"\n    Extract all billing details from this Indian tax invoice/cash bill.\n    RULES:\n    1. Extract vendor name (company title only, no phone numbers).\n    2. Extract only valid goods/services into the `items` list. DO NOT include addresses, phone numbers, or pincodes as items.\n    3. Read numeric amounts carefully. Do not invent items.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    response = client.models.generate_content(\n        model='gemini-2.5-flash',\n        contents=[\n            types.Part.from_bytes(data=contents, mime_type=mime_type),\n            prompt\n        ],\n        config=types.GenerateContentConfig(\n            response_mime_type=\"application/json\",\n            response_schema=ExtractedInvoice,\n            temperature=0.0\n        )\n    )\n    return response.text\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-02T22:34:10+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
