ling details extraction.\n\n\nThe initial approach returns a raw JSON string, which FastAPI will automatically wrap in quotes, causing an issue with JSON parsing on the frontend. This needs correction. Returning a `Response` object with the `application/json` media type will correctly return the raw JSON string and make it parseable in JavaScript. This will fix the endpoint's response handling.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/venv/bin/python3 -c \"\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom fastapi.responses import Response\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.post('/test-string')\ndef test_string():\n    return '{\\\"hello\\\": \\\"world\\\"}'\n\n@app.post('/test-response')\ndef test_response():\n    return Response(content='{\\\"hello\\\": \\\"world\\\"}', media_type='application/json')\n\nclient = TestClient(app)\nr1 = client.post('/test-string')\nprint('r1 text:', r1.text)\nprint('r1 json():', repr(r1.json()))\n\nr2 = client.post('/test-response')\nprint('r2 text:', r2.text)\nprint('r2 json():', repr(r2.json()))\n\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Test FastAPI response handling"}}]}
